  "Live position: pause between updates (ms)": "实时位置：两次更新之间的暂停（毫秒）",
  "ui_settings_from": "开启时间",
  "ui_settings_to": "结束时间",
  "ui_settings": "设置",
  "ui_settings_dnd_off_hint": "修改后的时间将在开启该模式时发送。",
  "Milliseconds the adapter waits after one answer before it asks for the robot position again. It is a pause, not a fixed rate: the next question goes out only once the previous answer has arrived, so the requests can never pile up and a slow connection simply slows the updates down instead. The default of 1500 ms comes from a measurement at a driving robot: it advances its own position only about every 3 seconds, so 95 percent of the requests in a 100 ms test returned the value they had already returned before. 1500 ms samples that roughly twice per update, which is enough not to skip a step. A shorter setting does not make the robot report more often - it only produces more requests, and the position it shows is on average about 1.5 seconds old whatever is configured here, because that is the robot's own update grid. 250 ms is the fastest allowed, kept well below the default so a model that updates faster than the measured one is not held back. Two limits apply automatically and cannot be undercut: while the robot stands still, and while it is only reachable through the Roborock cloud, the pause is at least 2 seconds. 0 switches the live position off; the robot is then only shown where the last map put it. Values from 1 to 30 are still read as the whole seconds this option used to count, so an existing setting keeps working - set a value of 250 or more to use the new unit.": "适配器在收到一次回答后，再次询问机器人位置前等待的毫秒数。这是一段暂停而不是固定节拍：只有上一个回答到达后才会发出下一个问题，因此请求永远不会堆积，连接慢时只会让更新变慢。默认的 1500 毫秒来自对行驶中机器人的实测：它大约每 3 秒才更新一次自身位置，因此在 100 毫秒的测试中，95% 的请求返回的都是此前已返回过的数值。1500 毫秒大约每次更新采样两次，足以不漏掉任何一步。设置得更短并不会让机器人上报得更频繁，只会产生更多请求；无论此处如何设置，所显示的位置平均都有约 1.5 秒的延迟，因为那是机器人自身的更新节奏。250 毫秒是允许的最快值，明显低于默认值，以免比实测机型更新更快的型号被拖慢。有两个自动生效且无法突破的下限：机器人静止时以及仅能通过 Roborock 云端访问时，暂停至少为 2 秒。0 表示关闭实时位置，机器人此时只显示在最后一次地图所标注的位置。1 到 30 的数值仍按此选项以前所计的整秒读取，使已有设置继续有效——若要使用新单位，请填入 250 或更大的数值。",
